{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Do not fear, Abram.</b> It turns out that when he killed the kings he feared lest his merits had diminished. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״You cleared thorns from the vineyard״ — ״Do not fear, I am a shield to you,״ and therefore we say מגן אברהם. And at the hour Isaac was bound, his soul flew away and ascended on high, and returned to his body and revived him — therefore he composed מחיה המתים. And it is found in the Midrash: when Isaac's soul flew away and ascended on high, it gazed upon the splendor of the Shekhinah, as it is written: ״לא יראני האדם וחי״, and therefore ״ותכהן עיניו מראות״. And at the hour Jacob saw the angels ascending and descending and accompanying him at every moment, they were giving thanks and praising the Holy One, blessed be He — therefore he composed האל הקדוש."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The subjects of the verbs התקין ('he composed') are ambiguous in the Hebrew; read here as Isaac composing מחיה המתים and Jacob composing האל הקדוש, following the flow of the passage."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:27.250494214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}